meta {
  name: Linked share
  seq: 30
}

docs {
  > Linked-item discovery and sharing for an agent (issue #481).
  >
  > `GET resource-flows/{resourceType}/{resourceId}/linked-share-candidates?userIds=a,b`
  > lists what the agent uses, per recipient, so the share dialog can offer
  > "Also share these items". `00-`…`07-` cover discovery (Dev items, items used
  > only by a called agent, Production copies of a published version, a sharer
  > who does not own an item, a stranger, a bad resource type, an unknown agent,
  > and Everyone-flagged items). `10-`…`21-` mirror what the dialog sends on
  > Save changes and read the result back (AC1–AC7).
  >
  > Prerequisites (Environment or Global Environment):
  > - `LINK_OWNER_TOKEN` — the agent owner's token.
  > - `LINK_SHARER_TOKEN` — an agent owner who does not own one linked item (AC5).
  > - `LINK_RECIPIENT_TOKEN`, `LINK_RECIPIENT_ID` — the person the agent is shared with.
  > - `LINK_SECOND_RECIPIENT_TOKEN`, `LINK_SECOND_RECIPIENT_ID` — the person used only
  >   for the toggle-off case (AC4).
  > - `LINK_STRANGER_TOKEN` — a tenant user with no access to the agent.
  > - `LINK_FLOW_ID` — an unpublished agent (Flow) referencing `LINK_DEV_CREDENTIAL_NAME`
  >   and a queue named `LINK_QUEUE_NAME`.
  > - `LINK_CALLING_FLOW_ID`, `LINK_CALLED_TOOL_NAME` — an agent calling another agent
  >   that uses that tool and nothing else does.
  > - `LINK_PUBLISHED_VERSION_ID`, `LINK_DEV_CREDENTIAL_ID`, `LINK_PROD_CREDENTIAL_ID`
  >   — a published chat agent version plus the Dev and Production ids of one credential
  >   it references (AC3).
  > - `LINK_QUEUE_ID` — the queue `LINK_FLOW_ID` references (AC2/AC7).
  > - `LINK_UNSHARED_QUEUE_ID` — another queue `LINK_FLOW_ID` uses that nothing here shares (AC4).
  > - `LINK_HIGHER_LEVEL_QUEUE_ID` — a queue `LINK_FLOW_ID` uses, seeded at Can edit (AC6).
  > - `LINK_NON_OWNED_CREDENTIAL_ID` — a credential the agent references that
  >   `LINK_SHARER_TOKEN`'s user does not own and holds no Owner row on (AC5).
  > - `LINK_EVERYONE_CREDENTIAL_ID` — a linked credential with Everyone on (AC7).
  >
  > Run the folder, not a single file: `10-`…`13-` seed the rows `11-`/`13-` read
  > back, `17-` seeds the Can edit row, and `21-` depends on `20-`.
}
